To optimize the search functionality and reduce latency, I have implemented a robust parallel fetching strategy and introduced a custom, schema-based data compression utility (`Toon`) for efficient client-side caching.

Here is the summary of the changes:
1.  **`utils/toon.ts`**: Created a new utility that implements a "Type-Object-Object-Notation" style packing algorithm. This separates keys from values, significantly reducing the memory footprint when caching arrays of complex objects like `ResearchPaper`.
2.  **`services/openalexService.ts`**: Integrated `Toon` to compress search results before storing them in the client-side cache (`openAlexCache`). This allows for more efficient memory usage and faster retrieval of cached search sessions.
3.  **`services/apiService.ts`**: Upgraded the search orchestration to use `Promise.allSettled` instead of `Promise.all`. This ensures that if one data source (e.g., OpenAlex) fails or times out, the application will still display results from other successful sources (e.g., arXiv), rather than failing completely.

